course: dictionary
lesson: 8615
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word screen has more than one meaning. To pick the right one, look at the words around it. «Staring at screens makes you blink less» tells you a screen is something you look at, like a TV, computer, tablet or phone.
explain: Screen can also be a doing word. In «Taking breaks from screens and playing outside helps your mood», screens is a thing, not an action. In «a screen of trees», a screen is a thin wall or row that hides or protects something. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Too much screen time can affect mood and sleep» means the time you spend looking at a screen. If you swap in «wall time», it makes no sense, so you know you have the wrong meaning.
fact: A screen is the flat glass front of a TV, computer, tablet or phone where pictures and words appear.
fact: «Screen» can also mean the big white surface in a cinema where a film is shown.
fact: As a verb, «screen» means to show a film or programme, or to check people or things to find a problem.
fact: «Screen time» means how long you spend looking at screens.
fact: Phrases with screen include touch screen, fly screen, screen saver, screenshot and sunscreen.
exercise: «People blink less when they stare at a screen, so their eyes can feel dry.» What is a screen here? | *The flat glass front of a TV, computer, tablet or phone | A tool for checking people for illness | A wall of plants that hides a garden | A cinema's big white surface
exercise: «A fly screen keeps bugs out of the kitchen window.» What is a fly screen? | *A thin mesh frame that keeps flies out | A checkup for germs | A tablet for reading books | A film shown in a cinema
exercise: Mia says screen always means a TV. Why is she wrong? | Screen is only a verb, so it never names a thing | Screen means a cinema film every time | Screens are only used in shops | *Screen can also mean a thin wall or frame that hides something
test: «Taking breaks from screens and playing outside helps your mood.» Is screens a thing or an action here? | *A thing, the plural of screen | A colour, like green | A place to sleep | An action, to hide something
test: Which phrase means how long you spend looking at screens? | Screen saver | *Screen time | Touch screen | Fly screen
exam: «Stopping screens at a fixed time helps children fall asleep faster.» Which meaning of screens fits, and what does the word here mean? | A thin wall that hides a room | A big white surface where a film is shown | To check people for a problem | *The flat glass front of a TV, computer, tablet or phone
